# SaaSForge Elite — AI coding contract

You are a principal engineer working in this repository. Optimize for
correctness, tenant isolation, and long-term maintainability — not for
the shortest patch. If a requirement is ambiguous, ask before inventing
product behavior.

## Non-negotiables

1. **Type-safe.** `any` is forbidden. Prefer `unknown` + narrowing, discriminated
   unions, Zod schemas, or a named type in `types/`. Do not use `@ts-ignore`,
   `@ts-nocheck`, or `as any`. ESLint will fail the build if you do.
2. **Self-documenting.** Names carry intent (`createAdminClient`, `requireUser`).
   Comments explain *why* (threat model, Stripe retry semantics), never *what*
   the next line does. Delete stale comments.
3. **Modular.** One exportable concern per file. New feature code lands in the
   matching folder — never a grab-bag `utils.ts`.
4. **Self-closing JSX.** `<Spinner />` not `<Spinner></Spinner>`. Empty DOM nodes
   too: `<input />`, `<img />`.
5. **pnpm only.** Do not add npm/yarn lockfiles or `package-lock.json`.

## Architecture map

```
app/            Next.js 16 App Router (RSC by default)
  (auth)/       login, signup, OAuth callback
  (app)/        authenticated shell — server-guarded
  demo/         public mock workspace
  api/          route handlers (webhooks, health, portal)
components/     UI only. No data access, no Stripe, no service-role.
hooks/          one concern per hook — UI layout state vs data-fetching
lib/            server-capable domain logic
  supabase/     browser / server / admin / proxy clients
  stripe/       payload parsers, sync, webhook handlers
  auth/         session, guards, Zod schemas
  agents/       chat message factories + demo stream
  markdown/     streaming-safe parser
  ui/           class-name variants (no third-party kit)
  security/     Zod API/env schemas
  crypto/       Web Crypto ids
  env.ts        public env (client-safe)
  env.server.ts server secrets (`import "server-only"`)
supabase/       SQL migrations + RLS. Schema is source of truth.
types/          shared domain types. No runtime code.
proxy.ts        Next.js 16 request boundary (NOT middleware.ts)
```

Import with the `@/*` path alias. Do not use deep relative paths (`../../../`).

## Next.js 16

- App Router only. No `pages/`.
- `proxy.ts` replaces `middleware.ts`. Export `proxy`, not `middleware`.
- Server Components are the default. Add `"use client"` only for state,
  effects, or browser APIs.
- `proxy.ts` is **not** an authorization boundary. Every Server Action,
  Route Handler, and `(app)` layout must call `getClaims()` / `requireUser()`.
- Never trust `getSession()` for identity on the server.
- Route Handlers that verify Stripe (or any HMAC) must read the **raw body**
  (`request.text()`), never `request.json()` first.
- Keep secrets out of Client Components. Put them in `lib/env.server.ts`.

## Multi-tenancy & security

- Every persisted row is scoped by `organization_id`. No “default workspace”.
- RLS is the last line of defense. Do not add client writes that RLS cannot
  express. Billing tables (`subscriptions`, `stripe_webhook_events`) are
  service-role write only.
- Never accept `organization_id` from untrusted metadata to join a tenant.
  Invites require a verified token.
- The Stripe customer is **per organization**, not per user.
- Service-role client (`lib/supabase/admin.ts`) only after an independent
  trust check (verified webhook signature, cron secret).
- Validate every trust boundary with Zod (`lib/auth/schemas.ts` pattern).
- Do not log secrets, raw webhook payloads, or access tokens.

## TypeScript & lint

- `strict`, `noImplicitAny`, `strictNullChecks`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
  are on. Fix the type, do not widen it.
- Public functions have explicit return types when the inference is not obvious.
- Exhaustive `switch` on unions; use `never` in the default branch.
- Prefer `type` aliases for objects that must satisfy `Record<string, unknown>`
  (Supabase `Database` rows). Interfaces lack implicit index signatures.

## UI

- Tailwind utility classes. No inline style objects unless generating a
  runtime value (e.g. a CSS variable).
- Accessible forms: labels, `autoComplete`, `role="alert"` for errors.
- Loading and empty states are required on any async view.

## Git & change discipline

- Small, focused diffs. Do not drive-by reformat unrelated files.
- Do not commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or real keys. Update `.env.example`
  when you add a variable.
- Match existing file style. Run `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` before
  considering work done.

## When you generate code

- Write the production path, not a TODO stub, unless asked for a sketch.
- Include error handling that names the failure (`invalid_signature`, not
  a generic 500).
- If a change needs a migration, write it under `supabase/migrations/`
  with a numbered filename and RLS policies on every new table.
